abstract: >-
  Jupyter notebook accompanying the tutorial article "From single-pixel imaging to scattered light
  imaging: a practical tutorial". It applies single-pixel imaging and compressive sensing to
  scattered light imaging (SLI) with binary Hadamard illumination patterns, using measured angular
  scattering profiles of two crossing human optic tract sections: canonical vs. Hadamard sampling,
  sparsity and incoherence, pattern ordering, iterative and learned linear reconstruction, noise
  robustness and fiber orientation maps from compressed data. Runs on the free Google Colab CPU runtime.
keywords:
  - single-pixel imaging
  - scattered light imaging
  - compressive sensing
  - Hadamard patterns
  - learned reconstruction
  - fiber orientation
  - neuroimaging
  - tutorial
